ProjectALife.DialogueShards["radio_13"] = {
{"r8_hor_note_in_my_own_hand","caller_story_horror",15,190,23,5,1,{"Orville","Note under my wiper Tuesday - folded once","June","What did it say?","Orville","Said back by dark, feed the calf, which is a thing I'd write","June","Is it something you wrote?","Orville","It's my hand, I'll set it beside a check stub and you couldn't tell 'em apart - the way I make a d, everything","Orville","I did not write it, and there ain't been a calf on this place in two years","June","Two years","Orville","Sold the last one in ninety-one, so it's a note I'd have wrote in about eighty-nine, in my hand, under my wiper, on the fourteenth of July","Orville","I got it in my shirt pocket right now - you want to see it? I'll bring it in, I'd like somebody to look at it that ain't me"}},
{"r8_hor_hound_sits_at_the_fence","caller_story_horror",15,190,1,5,1,{"Merle","My hound will run anything, rabbits, coon, a deer if I let her, and she don't quit","June","A good dog","Merle","Best I've had, and there's one field she won't go in - the forty on the far side of Echo Creek Road, the one that's growed up in broom sage","Merle","She'll run the whole line and get to that fence and sit down","June","Sits down at the fence","Merle","Sits - looks in, won't bark, won't whine, and she's a loud dog, she'll tell you about a squirrel for an hour","June","Have you walked it?","Merle","I went in a ways, brush is over your head in there - you can't see six foot","Merle","I come back out and she was still sat right there where I left her, and that's about all I want to say about that field"}},
{"r8_hor_buzzards_over_nothing","caller_story_horror",15,195,22,4,1,{"Dorsey","Buzzards circling a spot on the bottom ground, fifteen, twenty of 'em, high up, that slow wheel they do","June","They've had plenty to work with lately","Dorsey","They have, and that's why nobody looked twice the first day - you see buzzards now and you go the other way, that's just sense","Dorsey","Three days they stayed on that one spot, never come down","June","Never landed","Dorsey","Not one bird, three days, a buzzard don't circle three days - it comes down and eats and it's gone by dinner","June","Did you go look?","Dorsey","Two of us walked out there Thursday with rifles - cut corn stubble, flat as this table, you can see a can from a hundred yards","Dorsey","There's nothing on the ground at all, no carcass, no bones, no smell, not even flies","Dorsey","Birds are still up there tonight, you can hear 'em when the wind's right, and buzzards don't hardly make a sound, which is how I know how many there is"}},
{"r8_sad_paper_route_jar","caller_story_sad",15,190,20,2,1,{"June","You're on - take your time","Thelma","My grandson had a paper route, fifty-one customers in West Point, the morning paper, up at four thirty every day","June","That's early for a boy","Thelma","Thirteen, he never once asked me to wake him twice - set his own alarm and everything","Thelma","He kept the money in a peanut butter jar and counted it Friday nights at the kitchen table - out loud, in stacks","June","Saving for something?","Thelma","A dirt bike, he had a picture of it tore out of a magazine taped inside his closet door and he'd priced it out to the month","June","How close was he?","Thelma","Sixty-two dollars short, he'd have had it by October","Thelma","The jar's still on the shelf, I counted it Friday - I don't know why I did that, and then last Friday I did it again","June","What's his name?","Thelma","Junior, everybody called him Junior - his real name's Carl Ray Cobb and he'd have wanted me to say that on the radio"}},
{"r8_sad_names_we_never_used","caller_story_sad",15,195,0,4,1,{"Dee","Go ahead","Dorsey","My wife's expecting - was - is, I don't know how to say it, and that's not the call","Dee","Take whatever order you need","Dorsey","We had a list, on the back of an envelope, stuck in the phone book at the S's, that's where she kept it","Dee","Names","Dorsey","Eleven for a girl, three for a boy, 'cause she said boys are easy - she crossed out the ones my mother didn't like and then wrote 'em back in","Dee","Do you want to read them?","Dorsey","That's why I called and now I can't - give me a second","Dorsey","Ruth - Alma - Jeanette - six more, and the boys was Earl, after her daddy, and Wendell and one I can't make out, she wrote it going up the side","Dee","Ruth, Alma, Jeanette","Dorsey","Thank you for saying 'em, that's the first time anybody's said them out loud but us two in the dark"}},
{"r9_sil_d15_truck_he_knows","silence",15,60,0,23,1,{"Marty","Hold on, there's a truck pulling in the lot and I know that truck","Marty","Stand by, folks, don't touch your dial, I'll be right back","Marty","All right - I'm back, that was somebody I used to sell feed to, and he wanted to ask me something in a building instead of on a radio","Marty","I'm not going to tell you what he asked me - I'd like you to know that's a thing you can do - drive over and ask me in the building"}},
{"r2_d16_hollis_prays_callsigns","military",16,16,8,12,3,{"Reverend Hollis","Good morning, this is Hollis, from the little church on the Ekron road - Marty's kindly given me the Sunday hour, and asked me to keep it to an hour","Reverend Hollis","All week I've listened to the soldiers on his scanner, same as you - I don't know their names, I know what they call each other","Reverend Hollis","So this morning I'll pray the way they talk - Lord, keep Lockbox, out on the bridge, still saying the same hard words at the fifth pole","Reverend Hollis","Keep Hatchet and Anvil and Crowbar, keep Striker, who found out the fire channel answers - keep the boy at the Ekron firehouse who needed one person to believe him","Reverend Hollis","Keep the nine at the water plant, who are past our keeping, and the sergeant who called them every hour - give him somewhere to set it down","Reverend Hollis","And keep the specialist with the numbers on the back of his hand, whatever those numbers came to","Reverend Hollis","Over, that's how they close, and I think it's as good as amen - maybe better, it means somebody's still waiting on an answer"}},
{"r3_so_d16_hollis_first","sign_on",16,16,6,8,8,{"Marty","Good morning, it's Sunday, and we have a guest, which is a thing I never figured on saying from inside a feed store","Marty","Reverend Walter Hollis pastors the little church out on the Rosewood road - he walked here, four miles, at seventy-three years of age, and he has already asked for a chair","Reverend Hollis","Thank you, Marty, I asked for a chair because I'm seventy-three, good morning, everybody","Reverend Hollis","I'm not going to preach at you, I preached for forty years, and the congregation slept through thirty-nine of them","Reverend Hollis","I just thought that on a Sunday, somebody ought to say good morning to you like it's Sunday - so good morning - it's Sunday","Reverend Hollis","If you're a church person, I'll be back on in an hour with a few words - if you're not, I'll be back on in an hour anyway, and you're free to turn me off - the Lord and I have both been turned off before","Marty","He's with us all morning, I've been sent to find him a cushion"}},
{"r3_host_d16_hollis_tea","host",16,16,9,12,8,{"Reverend Hollis","Marty's given me the microphone for a few minutes, I'll try not to wear it out","Reverend Hollis","I'm not reading you a verse this morning, most of you know where to find them, and the ones that don't, I'm not going to catch you up over the radio","Reverend Hollis","I'll tell you what I did this week instead, I buried Earl Ogle in the churchyard on Tuesday, his wife Ada spelled me on the shovel","Reverend Hollis","Ada is eighty years old, she taught half the children in March Ridge to play piano, and she digs a better hole than I do","Reverend Hollis","When we finished, she said, 'Walter, don't you say anything over him - he'd hate it.' So I didn't","Reverend Hollis","We stood there till the shade came across, then she asked if I wanted a glass of tea, and I said yes - that's what I've got for you, somebody offered tea, and I said yes"}},
{"r3_sil_d16_scanner_holds","silence",16,30,22,4,1,{"99.6 FM","(Dead air, in the background the scanner stops on a channel and holds there, and nobody speaks on it - then it moves on)"}},
{"r4_sad_boy_mows_lawns","caller_story_sad",16,30,8,18,1,{"Caller - Kyle","Hi - I'm Kyle - I'm thirteen, I have a lawn business - had - have, six yards in Riverside, every Saturday","Marty","A businessman - go ahead, Kyle","Caller - Kyle","Mrs. Ogle's yard is the first one on Saturday, she pays five dollars and she always gives me a pop from her garage fridge","Caller - Kyle","Her house is empty now - I checked, her car's gone - nobody's there, so I don't know if she's coming back","Caller - Kyle","I pushed the mower over there this morning, I didn't start it - it's loud, it would bring them","Caller - Kyle","So I pulled the tall stuff by hand around her flower beds - the front part, the part people see, took all morning","Caller - Kyle","She doesn't have to pay me, I just didn't want her to come back and have it look like nobody lives there","Dee","(Dee opens her mouth and closes it)","Caller - Kyle","That's all, I have to go do the edges"}},
{"r5_host_feed_inventory_horn","host",16,80,0,23,1,{"Marty","People keep asking what's left at the feed store, so here's the inventory, honest as I can make it","Marty","Salt blocks, I have more salt blocks than any man in the history of Kentucky - mineral tubs, fly bait, a pallet of horse wormer, and forty bags of rabbit pellets","Dee","Tell them about the bicycle horn","Marty","There's a pink bicycle horn with a rubber bulb on my counter - it's been there six years, I ordered it by mistake and couldn't sell it for a nickel","Dee","He's marked it down four times, the tag's got four prices crossed out","Marty","If you've got a child who could use something silly right now, it's free - come get it - please - six years"}},
{"r5_obit_hollis_first_sunday","obituary",16,16,8,12,8,{"Marty","Good morning, it's Sunday, and I've asked a man to sit at this microphone who knows better what to say on a Sunday than I do","Reverend Hollis","Thank you, Marty, my name is Hollis, I've pastored the Methodist church here in March Ridge for nineteen years - that's where this transmitter came from, if you wondered","Reverend Hollis","Our building is still standing, but I won't ask anyone to come to it - I'll come to you, this way, on Sundays, for as long as Marty will have me","Reverend Hollis","People have sent names, I'll read them slowly, if you knew one, just stop where you are for a minute","Reverend Hollis","Orville Combs, of March Ridge, he mowed the church lawn for eleven years and never once let us thank him in the bulletin","Reverend Hollis","Jeannie Tolliver, of Rosewood, she taught Sunday school to the four-year-olds and kept raisins in her purse for emergencies","Reverend Hollis","Luis Ortega, of West Point, he came to our potluck exactly once, eight years ago - brought a pot of beans and stayed to wash every dish","Reverend Hollis","I don't have a sermon this morning, I have the names - let's let them be enough for today"}},
{"r8_hor_flowers_strange_grave","caller_story_horror",16,220,23,5,1,{"Roberta","I take care of the churchyard in March Ridge - well, nobody made me, I just do it","June","Go ahead","Roberta","There's a grave in the back corner from before all this - nineteen sixty-something, the stone's about wore off","Roberta","There's fresh flowers on it - every week - cut flowers, in a jar of water, water's clean","June","Somebody in the family, maybe","Roberta","There ain't a soul left in this county with a flower garden - everybody's growing beans and squash - I'd know","Roberta","Not from a garden either, a greenhouse, you can tell by the stems, cut square","June","I'd leave that jar where it sits","Roberta","Oh, I water it, whoever's doing it is doing something kind and I'm not about to be the one that stops it"}},
{"r8_hor_diesel_no_tracks","caller_story_horror",16,200,0,4,1,{"Doyle","Diesel idling on the gravel road below our place, every night, ten or eleven o'clock till about two","June","Idling, not moving?","Doyle","Sits there and idles - big one, you feel it in the floor, it's that kind of engine - truck, or a dozer maybe","Doyle","No headlights, that's the first wrong thing","June","And the second?","Doyle","I go down in the morning and there's no tracks - that's a wet gravel road with clay under it, a bicycle leaves a mark on it","Doyle","No tracks, no oil drip, no diesel smell, and I'd smell diesel, I run a farm","June","I'll say what I usually say, I'm not going to guess for you","Doyle","I don't want a guess, I want somebody two ridges over to tell me they hear it too, 'cause my wife don't hear it"}},
{"r8_hor_knew_the_grace","caller_story_horror",16,200,1,5,1,{"Dee","Go ahead, sir, you're on with Dee","Dorsey","We got a grace we say, my papaw made it up, it don't rhyme, it's got my grandmother's name in the middle of it","Dee","A family thing","Dorsey","Never been wrote down, never been said outside that kitchen table, three generations of us and that's it","Dorsey","Fella at our table Saturday said it with us, word for word - name and all","Dee","Did anybody else notice?","Dorsey","My mother did, she had ahold of my wrist before he got to the amen","Dee","What did you do?","Dorsey","Ate supper - what are you going to do, at a table, with kids sat there? We ate supper and he left in the morning","Dorsey","We don't say the grace out loud no more, we just sit a second, it ain't the same and I know it ain't"}},
{"r8_hor_check_marks_prayer_list","caller_story_horror",16,210,0,4,2,{"Reverend Hollis","Go ahead, it's late and I'm the only one awake in this building, so take your time","Roberta","We keep a prayer list on the board in the fellowship hall at March Ridge - names of the sick and the missing","Reverend Hollis","We keep one too","Roberta","Forty-some names, folks add 'em with the pencil on the string, it's been the same board since I was a girl","Roberta","Somebody's put check marks by some of the names","Reverend Hollis","Which ones?","Roberta","The dead ones, only the dead ones","Reverend Hollis","How many of those does the county know about?","Roberta","Not all of 'em, that's why I'm on the radio at two in the morning - there's four checked that we didn't know was gone, and I've asked around, and they are","Reverend Hollis","Then somebody knows the county better than the county does - I'd want that board took down","Roberta","I took the pencil off the string, that's all I could bring myself to do - the names are still up"}},
{"r8_hor_sale_barn_pens","caller_story_horror",16,200,1,5,1,{"Otho","Sale barn at the county line, I've sold stock out of that barn thirty years","June","Go ahead","Otho","There's stock in the pens, somebody penned up cattle and hogs and left 'em, which happens now, folks run off","Otho","They're alive, standing up, on their feet, eyes clear, hungry, but alive","Otho","There ain't a sound in that barn","June","Hungry cattle are loud","Otho","Hungry cattle will deafen you, hogs are worse - you cannot walk in a sale barn and not get hollered at by every pen","June","But not this time","Otho","I opened the gates and drove 'em out to grass and not one of 'em made a sound the whole time - not going out the door, not in the lot","Otho","I fed 'em and I come home, I done the right thing and I've not felt right since"}},
{"r8_hor_bees_left_the_honey","caller_story_horror",16,210,22,4,1,{"Estill","I keep bees, nine hives out behind the garden, been at it since seventy-four","June","Go ahead","Estill","They're gone - all nine, not a bee on the place","June","Did something get in them?","Estill","Nothing's tore up, no wax moth, no mice, no bear - lids on, straps on, everything how I left it","Estill","And the honey's still in 'em, that's what I can't square, nine hives of honey","June","They left the honey","Estill","A swarm takes what it can carry and a robbed hive gets cleaned out by everybody in the county - this is neither one","Estill","There's no dead bees on the bottom boards - not one, in twenty years I've never opened a box without a few dead bees in it","Estill","I'll get the honey off in the fall, I'm not in a hurry to go out there and take the lids off again, is all"}},
{"r8_sad_ring_wrong_hand","caller_story_sad",16,200,22,4,1,{"Dee","Go ahead, you're on with me","Coy","I gave a class ring back to a woman Tuesday - her boy's","Dee","You knew him?","Coy","Worked with him, ninety-one graduate, the ring's got the red stone and the year on the side - big heavy thing","Dee","How did she take it?","Coy","She put it on, right there in the yard, and it wouldn't stay on her finger, so she put it on her thumb","Coy","And then she said thank you for driving out - twice, she said it twice and asked if I wanted a glass of water","Dee","Did you take it?","Coy","I did, I sat on her porch and drank a glass of water and we talked about the heat","Coy","That's all of it... I don't know what I'm asking anybody for, I just haven't been able to eat since Tuesday","Dee","You don't have to be asking for anything, I'm here a while yet"}},
{"r8_sad_the_number_is_five","caller_story_sad",16,210,22,4,2,{"June","You're on ninety-nine six","Merle","Five","June","Go on","Merle","I've buried five since the sixth, on this place, in the corner past the garden, where the ground's soft","June","Five people","Merle","I'm not telling you for sympathy, I want to be plain about that, 'cause I know how it sounds at this hour","Merle","I'm telling you so the number's somewhere besides my head","June","Five, on your place, past the garden","Merle","That's it, that's all I want","June","I've got it wrote down, five since the sixth - it's on paper in front of me","Merle","All right then, I'll get off the line and let somebody else on"}},
{"r9_host_d16_dee_wont_diagnose","host",16,50,0,23,1,{"Dee","I need to say something about what I can and can't do out of this chair - I took eleven calls yesterday and I got about seven of them wrong","Dee","I can't tell you if it's appendicitis, I can tell you where to press and what it means if it hurts worse when you take your hand off - that is not the same thing and I'm not going to pretend it is","Dee","What I can do is tell you what to watch for, and when to quit watching and come find me - those are the two useful things I've got and I'll give them out all day","Marty","Tell them the part you told me in the truck","Dee","If I say come find me, come find me - don't wait till morning to be polite, I have sat with people who waited till morning to be polite","Marty","March Ridge, the feed store, any hour there's a light on - she means it, and she'll be ill with you if you don't"}},
{"r2_d17_church_drivers_turned","military",17,24,8,18,1,{"Keystone-6","Hatchet, Keystone-6, at the outer barrier on Highway 60, I have a relief convoy, twelve trucks, food and medicine for inside the line, over","Hatchet-6","Keystone-6, Hatchet-6, nobody told us you were coming - how does it cross, over?","Keystone-6","The plan is we set pallets down halfway between the barriers and back off a mile - your people come forward and carry it in, over","Hatchet-6","And the civilians who see pallets of food sitting in the road, over?","Keystone-6","That's why you'll be covering it, over","Hatchet-6","I have nineteen soldiers covering eleven miles, the first family that sees baby formula in the road runs for it, and my order says we fire, over","Keystone-6","Stand by","Keystone-6","Hatchet, Keystone-6, higher has turned the convoy around - cargo goes back to Elizabethtown, half these drivers are church volunteers who drove down from Ohio, over","Hatchet-6","Tell them thank you for the drive, tell them nobody inside will ever know they came - Hatchet-6, out"}},
{"r3_ins_d17_brace_corners","instruction",17,30,0,23,1,{"Marty","A word about fences, since I sold most of the fencing in this end of the county and I feel responsible","Marty","Woven wire, the kind you'd use for goats, will hold them back a while if the posts are set deep - barbed wire alone won't, they walk right into it and don't care","Marty","What pulls a fence down is weight, five or six of them leaning, so the corner posts matter more than the wire does - Brace your corners","Marty","An electric fence charger hooked to a car battery does nothing to them - I tested it - don't ask me how","Marty","Chain link is good until it isn't, if they're stacking up against it, you don't have a fence anymore, you have a clock - leave before it runs out"}},
{"r8_hor_whippoorwill_two_forty","caller_story_horror",17,220,1,5,1,{"Faye","You'll think this is nothing, it's a bird, I know it's a bird","June","Tell it anyway","Faye","Whippoorwill out back of the house, calls at twenty of three - I've looked at the clock nine nights running","Faye","Twenty of three on the dot every night, and it calls seven times and quits","June","Seven","Faye","Seven, my mamaw used to say count 'em, it's how many years till you marry - which is a foolish thing to put in a child's head","Faye","Anyway, I'm fifty-eight years old and I lay there counting a bird","June","I'd count it too","Faye","There ain't been a cricket out there in a week - that's the other thing, just the one bird at twenty of three"}},
{"r8_hor_hammer_on_iron","caller_story_horror",17,220,0,4,1,{"Talmadge","Hammer on iron, coming up out of the quarry - small hammer, ball peen, I'd say","June","Somebody working down there?","Talmadge","That's what a man hopes, except it ain't work, work's got a rhythm and then a stop - this has got a rhythm and no stop","Talmadge","Five hits, wait, five hits, wait - hours of it","June","Five","Talmadge","Always five, I sat with a watch and put marks on a board and I got sixty-some of 'em before I felt stupid and went to bed","June","Five hits is a signal in some places - Miners tap","Talmadge","It is, my papaw worked a mine in Harlan County and he'd tell you the same - that's what's got hold of me","Talmadge","'Cause if a fella's tapping, he's waiting on somebody to tap back - and I ain't going down in that quarry to tap back"}},
{"r8_hor_single_file_fence","caller_story_horror",17,220,23,5,1,{"Talmadge","I got in the old fire tower on the state ground - steps are rotten, don't nobody do what I did","June","Noted","Talmadge","You can see the whole east side of the county off that thing - I went up for an hour and I stayed three","Talmadge","There's a line of 'em walking a fence, single file, following the fence row","June","How many?","Talmadge","I don't know, it was a mile of fence and they was on all of it - spaced out, ten, fifteen foot apart, one behind the other","June","Going which way?","Talmadge","North, the whole time I watched, nobody stopped, nobody crossed over, and there's gaps in that fence they could've gone through","Talmadge","They stayed on the fence, like it was a road","June","I'm going to leave that as a line of people walking north","Talmadge","That's what I'd call it too, somebody ought to know it's a mile long, is all"}},
{"r8_sad_smudge_on_the_card","caller_story_sad",17,220,20,2,1,{"Marty","Line's open","Reba","I made my grandmother's cornbread Sunday, I've got her card for it, the index card, in her hand","Marty","How'd it come out?","Reba","Not like hers, it never is - there's something she didn't write down and she's been dead since eighty-eight so I'll never know what","Marty","There's always something they didn't write down","Reba","There's a grease thumbprint on the corner of that card - hers, from her thumb","Marty","I've got one of them cards too - my mother's","Reba","Then you know, I set it on the counter Sunday and I got flour on it and I about had a fit - wiped at it with my apron and made it worse","Marty","Is the print still there?","Reba","It's there, I've quit taking the card out of the box - I copied it over on a new card and I use the new one now","Reba","So there's two cards, and that's how I've solved it, and I'm fifty-four years old"}},
{"r9_ins_d17_boiling_gets_sloppy","instruction",17,70,8,20,1,{"Marty","Boiling water, you know how to boil water, and that is exactly the problem - second week everybody knows how, third week everybody gets sloppy in the same three places","Dee","One - the lid, rolling boil a full minute, then cover it - if you leave it open on the stove to cool all afternoon you have made a nice warm bath for the very thing you just killed","Dee","Two - the dipper - clean water, dirty dipper - hang one cup by the bucket and that cup does not touch the ground - not once, not for a second, not while you answer the door","Dee","Three - your hands - wash before you dip, not after","Marty","And keep them apart, boiled in one container, waiting in another, and don't you ever put the same lid on both","Dee","If you only take one thing off of this, take the dipper - it's always the dipper"}},
{"r3_so_d18_deacon_rooster","sign_on",18,24,5,6,1,{"Marty","It's {time}, and if you heard a rooster just then under my voice, that's not a sound effect - a man traded me a rooster yesterday","Marty","I didn't want a rooster, I wanted a car battery - what I got was a rooster and an apology","Marty","His name is Deacon, I've had him eighteen hours, and he's been awake longer than I have for every one of them","Marty","Dee says he's going to get us all killed - Dee has a point - Deacon has a stew pot in his future if he keeps it up","Marty","Good morning, ninety-nine point six - Deacon says get up"}},
{"r3_host_d18_fall_garden","host",18,30,9,17,1,{"Marty","Here's something useful, for a change, it's getting on toward August, which means it's time to put in a fall garden, if you've got a yard with any sun in it","Marty","I have seed, the rack by the door, turnips, collards, mustard greens, bush beans, and a whole case of lettuce nobody bought in the spring","Marty","Turnips and collards now, and they'll carry you into November - beans now, and you'll pick in September if the rain holds","Marty","The seed is free - come in daylight - take what you'll plant, not what you'll hoard - I'll know, I'll know because Dee will be standing there","Dee","I will be standing there","Marty","And plant it out back, where it can't be seen from the road - a nice straight row of beans is an advertisement"}},
{"r3_wx_d18_mower_belt_window","weather",18,28,5,10,1,{"Marty","Weather this morning is sunny and ninety, like nothing happened - that's how July apologizes","Marty","Last night's storm put a limb through the front window of the store and laid the antenna halfway over, which is why some of you lost me around ten - a man named Harlan from down the road helped me stand it back up in the dark","Marty","There are trees down across the Rosewood road by the church, both lanes - walking, you can climb over, driving, you're not getting through","Marty","The storm stirred them up, or it seemed to, more moving on the road after midnight than I've seen in a week - watch the tree lines today","Marty","Two inches in the rain gauge... and a good bit more on my floor, through that broken window"}},
{"r4_sad_dee_scissors_name","caller_story_sad",18,30,22,23,1,{"Dee","No calls, so you're getting me - try not to switch over to the static","Dee","When I finished nursing school my mother had my bandage scissors engraved - Deanna Price, RN Cost her eleven dollars at the jewelry counter","Dee","I lost them at work in the first month, some other nurse walked off with them - that happens, everybody steals your scissors","Dee","Mama was so mad she drove to the hospital to ask about them - I wanted to crawl under the nurses' station","Dee","Today a man came by the station with a bag of medical supplies he'd pulled out of a car on the Rosewood road - gauze, tape, a blood pressure cuff","Dee","And a pair of bandage scissors - engraved - not mine, somebody named Karen Lutz, L.P.N","Dee","Somebody's mother paid eleven dollars for that, probably, I'm using them - I'm going to keep them clean","Dee","Karen, if you're out there, I've got your scissors, I'm not giving them back, everybody steals your scissors","Marty","(Marty doesn't make a joke, he lets Dee have the quiet)"}},
{"r8_hor_tone_on_the_hour","caller_story_horror",18,240,0,4,1,{"Dwight","There's a carrier down at the low end of the dial - been there four nights","June","Is it a station?","Dwight","It's a tone, same tone, about eleven seconds, and then it quits, on the hour, right on the hour, every hour","Dwight","I timed it against my watch three nights, it don't drift - whatever's making it has got good power and a clock","June","That could be a transmitter somebody left on a timer","Dwight","That's what I'd say too, except last night it went twice - once on the hour and once at twenty after","June","Twenty after","Dwight","Twenty after, and tonight it was on the hour and twenty after and twenty of - it's filling in, I'm going to leave that right there"}},
{"r8_hor_pager_in_the_wall","caller_story_horror",18,240,23,5,1,{"Rex","There's a pager going off in the wall of the clinic in Muldraugh - the break room wall","Dee","I worked that clinic - which wall?","Rex","Behind the lockers, you can hear it plain as day, a little chirp, three and quit","Dee","Batteries in those things last a good while, that much I know","Rex","Sure, but somebody's got to be paging it, don't they? Something's got to be sending","Dee","The phone system's down, the whole exchange is down, I've tried it","Rex","Then who's calling? Every twenty minutes, all night, somebody's calling a doctor that ain't there","Dee","I want that to be a machine stuck on a loop in a building in Louisville","Rex","So do I, I pulled the lockers out and there ain't a pager behind 'em - I want to be real clear about that part"}},
{"r8_hor_answers_before_i_key","caller_story_horror",18,240,0,4,1,{"Dwight","There's a fella works nineteen most nights, good copy, strong signal, calls himself Tuesday","June","Tuesday","Dwight","That's his handle, which, all right, people pick what they pick, mine's Rabbit and I'm forty-nine years old","Dwight","He answers before I let go of the key","June","Before you finish","Dwight","Before I finish, you can't do that, June, the set won't do it, you're deaf while you're keyed, that's how the thing works","Dwight","So he's answering a question he ain't heard yet, three, four times a night","June","Are the answers right?","Dwight","Every time, I quit asking him anything - now I just listen to him answer other people, and he's doing it to them too"}},
{"r8_hor_handle_wrong_stress","caller_story_horror",18,240,0,4,1,{"Talmadge","My handle's Deadeye, it's a joke, I can't hit a barn - everybody on nineteen calls me it","June","All right","Talmadge","Somebody says it back wrong","June","Wrong how?","Talmadge","The weight's on the back half - dead-EYE, nobody says it like that - you wouldn't, you'd put it on the front, it's just how your mouth does it","Talmadge","Like somebody seen it wrote down and never heard it said","June","That's a fine thing to notice","Talmadge","I got a lot of hours on a radio and not much else to do with 'em - and every night about two he says it, dead-EYE, you got your ears on","Talmadge","I don't come back on him, but I'll tell you what, I've quit saying my own handle out loud, and I miss it - foolish thing to miss"}},
{"r8_hor_river_at_a_count","caller_story_horror",18,240,0,4,1,{"Woodrow","I've been going down to the Ohio to watch it - don't ask me why a man does that, I couldn't tell you","Dee","A lot of people are going to the river","Woodrow","There's things coming down it, everybody knows that - I'm not calling about that, I've got no stomach to talk about that","Woodrow","It's the timing of 'em","Dee","The timing","Woodrow","One about every ninety seconds, I sat with a watch Saturday for two hours, ninety seconds, give or take a few","Dee","That's a current thing, maybe, something upstream letting go a little at a time","Woodrow","That's what I want, that's exactly what I want it to be, a snag or a bridge piling holding things back","Woodrow","Two hours is eighty of 'em, that's the number I keep, eighty, and I'm telling you so it's wrote down somewhere besides my head"}},
{"r8_sad_four_pieces_short","caller_story_sad",18,240,23,5,1,{"June","Go ahead, you're on","Virgil","Me and my brother had a puzzle going on the card table - one of them thousand piece ones, a lighthouse","June","How far did you get?","Virgil","We'd been at it since spring, twenty minutes here, twenty minutes there, we wasn't in a hurry about it","Virgil","I finished it Thursday","June","By yourself","Virgil","Took me four days, and I'll tell you what I did the whole time, is I kept turning around to hand him a piece","Virgil","He done the edges, he always done the edges and I done the sky, that was how we split it up without ever saying so","June","Did it come out?","Virgil","Four pieces short, four holes in the water at the bottom - they're under that house somewhere, or in the dog, or they was never in the box","Virgil","I left it up on the table, nobody's said nothing about it and nobody's moved it, so"}},
{"r8_sad_attendance_board","caller_story_sad",18,250,19,1,1,{"Reverend Hollis","Go ahead, friend, I've got the rest of the night","Roberta","The board in the vestibule at March Ridge, the one with the little slots - attendance, offering, attendance last year","Reverend Hollis","Every church in the county's got one","Roberta","Ours still says the Fourth, a hundred and nine, offering was two hundred and forty-one dollars and some change","Reverend Hollis","A hundred and nine's a good Sunday","Roberta","It was Fourth of July, we had the dinner on the grounds after - everybody come, even the ones that don't","Reverend Hollis","And nobody's changed the numbers","Roberta","Who'd change 'em to what? There's nine of us meeting in the fellowship hall now and I'm not putting a nine up on that board","Reverend Hollis","No, leave it at a hundred and nine","Roberta","That's what I thought you'd say and it's why I called you instead of my sister - anyway, it's a nice board - Walnut"}},
{"r9_trade_d18_two_men_one_pump","trade",18,60,9,16,1,{"Marty","Two men want the same water pump and I have made a mess of it, so I'm going to fix it on the air and then we'll have a rule out of it","Marty","Erskine called Tuesday about the pump at the old Wickham place - Lonzo called Tuesday about the same pump, I told them both to go get it","Caller - Erskine","We met in the driveway, Marty","Caller - Lonzo","We did, and nobody got shot, so","Marty","So here's the rule and it's a dull one, first call gets it - I read the first call and only the first call - there is no bidding on this radio, you want to outbid a man, you do that to his face and not through me","Caller - Erskine","Lonzo's got kids in the house, he can have the pump","Caller - Lonzo","Well, now I don't want it","Marty","You're both taking the pump - Erskine's got the truck, Lonzo's got the pipe - go halves and argue about it later, that's my ruling and I'm the whole court around here"}},
{"r3_sf_d19_red_pickup","sign_off",19,28,21,23,1,{"Marty","We're going off early tonight, the diesel's low, and the young man who's been hauling it from Rosewood hasn't come by in four days","Marty","He's probably fine, he's probably found a better customer - I'd understand that, I'm terrible at haggling","Marty","Count your people, check your locks, and if you see a tall boy in a blue ball cap with milk jugs rattling in the back of a little red pickup, tell him Marty says hello","Marty","Good night"}},
{"r3_host_d19_deacon_rehomed","host",19,30,0,23,1,{"Dee","Update on Deacon the rooster, since six people on nineteen have asked","Marty","Seven","Dee","Seven - Deacon crowed at four-thirty yesterday morning, and two of them came up the road into the lot to see about it","Marty","I handled it","Dee","Marty handled it with a posthole digger, and Deacon now lives with a family down past the church who have a proper coop with a proper roof and no radio station attached","Marty","He is not in a pot, I want that clear - several of you asked about the pot","Dee","Several of you are hungry, and I don't blame you one bit"}},
{"r3_host_d19_buster_home","host",19,30,16,21,1,{"Caller - Rhonda","Breaker one-nine, is the radio on? This is Rhonda, in Riverside - I just wanted to tell somebody something good","Marty","Rhonda, you've got the whole county - go ahead","Caller - Rhonda","My dog came home - Buster, he's been gone since the first night, he walked up on the porch this afternoon like he'd just been down to the store","Caller - Rhonda","He's got a tick on his ear big as a grape and he smells like a creek bottom, and I've been holding onto him for two hours","Marty","Rhonda, that's the best news anybody's brought this radio all week, and I'm not saying that to be nice","Dee","Pull that tick with tweezers, straight up, slow, don't burn it","Caller - Rhonda","Yes ma'am, he won't let me put him down long enough","Marty","Then don't put him down, everybody, Buster's home"}},
{"r3_ins_d19_old_pills","instruction",19,30,0,23,1,{"Dee","People keep asking whether expired medicine is any good, short answer: most of it, mostly, for a good while","Dee","Pills that stayed dry and sealed hold up a long time - aspirin that smells like vinegar is done - throw it out","Dee","Anything liquid, anything that's supposed to live in a refrigerator, insulin, eye drops, the pink stuff for kids' ear infections, that goes bad in this heat - use it first or lose it","Dee","Don't take a stranger's pills just because the bottle says what you need - you don't know what's in that bottle now, people put things in the wrong bottles when the world was fine","Dee","And write down every pill you take, and when, on the wall, on your arm, I don't care where - you'll forget - everybody forgets"}},
{"r8_hor_open_mic_no_room","caller_story_horror",19,260,1,5,1,{"Dee","Go ahead, you're on with me","Rex","Somebody's got a mic keyed open on nineteen, all night, most nights this week","Dee","Stuck button, probably, it happens, somebody sits on it","Rex","When that happens you hear the room, kids, a TV, a fan, a woman yelling at somebody to get off it - you hear a house","Dee","And this?","Rex","Nothing, Dee, not a footstep or a chair creak, and a mic picks up a man breathing across a room","Dee","So the mic's in an empty place","Rex","Something's holding that key down - six hours, something's got to be holding it","Dee","I'm staying off nineteen and using twenty-one for a while, that's all I'm saying","Rex","Yeah, it's what I'm doing too - that's why I'm on a broadcast band at two in the morning talking to a nurse"}},
{"r8_sad_bingo_cards_set_out","caller_story_sad",19,260,19,1,1,{"June","Go ahead, hon","Nell","I called bingo at the home in Rosewood - Tuesdays and Fridays, two o'clock, in the dayroom","June","For how long?","Nell","Nine years, I've got the cage and the little wooden balls in my car right now, they're mine, I bought 'em","Nell","The cards are still set out on them tables, twenty-two of 'em, with the corn kernels in the cups beside 'em","June","You've been back in there","Nell","Once, it's quiet in a way that a building oughtn't be - I got the cage and I come out","Nell","Mr. Buckner used to holler bingo when he didn't have it - every single game, nine years of that man hollering bingo with nothing on his card","June","Nine years","Nell","I'd say Roy, read me your numbers, and he'd laugh - and I'd go on calling - anyway","Nell","If anybody's got old folks with 'em and wants a bingo cage, it's in my trunk on Tanner Road and it's free"}},
{"r9_host_d19_keyed_up_a_threat","host",19,60,0,23,1,{"Marty","Somebody keyed up on nineteen last night and told me to quit saying out loud where folks are meeting to trade - he was not friendly about how he put it","Marty","I'm going to answer him the one time and then I'm done with it - I don't know who you are and I'm not going to stand here and guess on the radio","Marty","What changes is trades happen in daylight, out in the open, two to a side, and I name the place that morning","Marty","What stays the same, I keep reading them, folks got to eat, and a man on a radio ain't why there's bad people here","Dee","And if you get somewhere and it feels wrong, leave - there's no rule anywhere that says you have to finish a trade you started","Marty","Leave, nobody's grading you on it"}},
{"r2_d20_weather_tomatoes","military",20,30,5,8,1,{"Hatchet-7","All stations, Hatchet-7, weather for {date}, cloud cover broken, wind out of the west, light - temperature about eighty-eight by noon, over","Hatchet-7","The river's down another foot, fog in the low ground until seven - no change to the line, over","Hatchet-7","For whoever is still at TCP 2, the tomatoes behind the church are ripe - take them before the birds do - Hatchet-7, out"}},
{"r3_host_d20_mouse_on_shoe","host",20,30,10,19,1,{"Marty","Dolly brought a mouse into the office this morning and laid it at Dee's feet","Dee","On my shoe, she laid it on my shoe","Marty","In cat, that's about the highest honor there is, she has never brought me a thing in nine years","Dee","I think it means she's decided I'm staying","Marty","I think it means she's decided you can't hunt","Dee","Well, she's not wrong - thank you, Dolly"}},
{"r3_ins_d20_door_marks","instruction",20,30,0,23,1,{"Marty","Some of you have started marking the houses you've already been through - that's smart, I'd like us all to use the same marks, so they mean something to the next person","Marty","Chalk or spray paint, beside the front door, eye level - one slash means somebody's been in, cross it into an X when the place is cleaned out, nothing left","Marty","Put the date under it, just the month and the day, a mark without a date is a guess","Marty","If there are dead inside that couldn't be dealt with, draw a circle around the whole thing - a circle means don't","Marty","And if somebody's still living there, they'll let you know - you won't need a mark for that"}},
{"r3_mb_d20_seed_packet","music_bridge",20,30,9,17,1,{"Marty","Nothing to play, so here's the back of a seed packet - Kentucky Wonder pole beans","Marty","'Plant one inch deep, four inches apart, after danger of frost - Provide support - pick when pods are firm and snap easily'","Marty","Provide support - pick when things snap easily, that's the best wisdom I've got today, and it came in a paper envelope for thirty-nine cents","Marty","Back to it"}},
{"r5_trade_goat_priscilla","trade",20,120,9,16,1,{"Marty","Trading Post - Ronnie, you're on","Caller - Ronnie","Marty, I've got a Nubian nanny goat in milk - real good-natured, she ate my clothesline, but good-natured","Marty","What are you after?","Caller - Ronnie","A car battery that holds a charge, and a bag of goat feed, if anybody's got one","Marty","I'll put in the feed myself, if she's going to a family with little ones","Dee","And if you're thinking goat's milk for a baby, talk to me first - it can be done, but not straight from the goat into the bottle","Caller - Ronnie","Noted, the Riverside boat ramp, the gravel lot, eight in the morning - her name's Priscilla, she doesn't answer to it, but that's her name","Marty","Priscilla the goat, eight AM, the gravel lot at the Riverside boat ramp - hide your laundry"}},
{"r5_joke_rhonda_pta_minutes","caller_joke",20,150,17,22,1,{"Caller - Rhonda","This is Rhonda Mayhew, president of the Riverside Elementary PTA, and I'm calling our monthly meeting to order on the air","Marty","Go right ahead, Madam President","Caller - Rhonda","Present: me, the treasurer, and my sister, who isn't a member but brought the lantern","Caller - Rhonda","Old business, the bake sale is postponed - the fall carnival is postponed, the dunk tank has a family of raccoons living in it","Caller - Rhonda","New business - lock your doors and count your children twice before bed","Caller - Rhonda","Forty-one dollars in the treasury, and a bread bag full of pop tabs. That's the report. Somebody move we adjourn, please","Marty","I'll second it, if that's allowed","Caller - Rhonda","It is not allowed, you don't have a child at Riverside Elementary - but the motion carries - meeting adjourned"}},
{"r5_trade_warning_irvington_elevator","trade",20,200,9,16,2,{"Marty","I need to take a minute out of the Trading Post for something I'm not glad to say","Marty","Two days ago a man went to meet a trade at the Irvington grain elevator - gas for a chainsaw, there was no gas, there were three men waiting behind the scale house","Dee","He walked eleven miles to get here, split lip, two cracked ribs, they took his truck and his boots","Marty","He's alright, he's asleep in the storeroom right now, so if we sound quiet, that's why","Marty","No more trades at the Irvington elevator on this station - if somebody offers you a meeting there, now you know why not","Dee","And if a trade sounds better than anything you've heard all week, don't call it luck - somebody's baiting you","Marty","The Trading Post will be open again tomorrow, tonight I don't have the stomach for it"}},
{"r5_trade_salt_for_hens_ida","trade",20,120,9,16,1,{"Marty","Ida Branham's on the line, and I've known this woman twenty years, so everybody behave","Caller - Ida","Marty, I've got six laying hens, and I'm fixing to butcher a hog when it cools off - I need salt, a lot of salt","Marty","Ida, you have called the one man in Knox County who has nothing but salt","Caller - Ida","I know it, that's why I called - how many blocks for six hens?","Marty","I'll give you salt till you tell me to stop","Caller - Ida","You'll give me salt till I've got a hernia, is what you'll do - front of your store, noon tomorrow, have a hand truck","Marty","Six hens, noon, out front of Colburn Feed, I'll have the hand truck - I've got four of those too"}},
{"r5_host_sleep_argument","host",20,130,0,23,1,{"Dee","Marty, when did you sleep last?","Marty","The air is not the place for this conversation","Dee","The air is the only place you listen, everybody, I've worked two whole night shifts, and he's been in that chair for both of them","Marty","I got up for the percolator","Dee","Walking to coffee is not sleep, Marty","Marty","It's close to sleep if you do it slow enough","Dee","He's lying down now, I'm going to stand right here until he does - talk amongst yourselves"}},
{"r5_joke_vernon_draft","caller_joke",20,200,17,22,1,{"Caller - Vernon","Marty, my house has developed a little bit of a draft","Marty","Weatherstrip the door, Vernon, I've got the foam kind in aisle two","Caller - Vernon","The door's fine, the door's standing right there, locked tight, deadbolt and all","Marty","Then where's the draft coming from?","Caller - Vernon","The wall next to the door - it's gone, a pickup came through it the other night","Marty","Good Lord, who was driving?","Caller - Vernon","Either one of them, or somebody from Louisville, hard to tell from how he parked"}},
{"r5_obit_marty_brinkley_staples","obituary",20,150,6,21,1,{"Marty","I'd like to read one of my own today, if you'll let me","Marty","Walter Brinkley ran the other feed store, in Rosewood, for twenty-six years he undercut me on sweet feed by a dime, and I undercut him on fence staples by a nickel","Marty","We did not speak, we'd see each other at the co-op meeting and nod like two bulls across a fence","Marty","On the tenth, with the phones cutting in and out, he called my store - first time in twenty-six years","Marty","He said, 'Colburn, you still got fence staples?' I said I did - he said, 'Knock another nickel off, people are going to need them.' And the line went","Marty","Well, Walt, everything in my store is free now - beat that"}},
{"r5_joke_tim_prettiest_voice","caller_joke",20,200,18,22,1,{"Caller - Tim","Um, hi, this is for Dee - Dee, you've got the prettiest voice on the radio","Dee","Tim, I'm the only woman on the radio","Caller - Tim","Still counts","Dee","How old are you, Tim?","Caller - Tim","Nineteen","Dee","Tim, your mama called this station last week about your poison ivy - she gave your age, it was not nineteen","Caller - Tim","Oh no","Dee","Calamine, clean socks, and go to bed - goodnight, Tim"}},
{"r5_obit_caller_juanita_motel_key","obituary",20,150,8,21,1,{"Caller - Rick","Marty, I drove a truck for twenty years, I want to say something for Juanita, at the diner by the truck stop on 31W","Marty","Go on, Rick","Caller - Rick","She called every driver 'hon.' Every one, even the ones who didn't deserve it","Caller - Rick","When a man came in looking like he'd fall asleep at the wheel, she'd bring his check with a motel key on it - the room next door, she'd paid for it","Caller - Rick","You'd try to pay her back and she'd say, 'Pay for somebody else's, hon'","Caller - Rick","Her name was Juanita Ybarra, I just wanted it said out loud once","Marty","Juanita Ybarra, thank you, Rick"}},
{"r5_joke_duane_bomb_shelter","caller_joke",20,300,17,22,1,{"Caller - Duane","Marty, my daddy built a bomb shelter in our backyard in nineteen sixty-two - poured the concrete himself","Marty","Well, Duane, that must be paying off now","Caller - Duane","I went down there for the first time in thirty years - it's stocked","Marty","With what?","Caller - Duane","Nineteen sixty-two, canned goods from nineteen sixty-two, a Geiger counter, a crank radio that won't crank, and a case of shells for a rifle Daddy sold in sixty-five","Caller - Duane","There's a jar of instant coffee, too, I tried it, it tastes like the Cuban Missile Crisis","Marty","Duane, bring me that coffee - I'm serious"}},
{"r5_host_wendell_arrives","host",20,120,0,23,1,{"Marty","For those who've asked, yes, the dog that followed Dee back from the creek is staying","Dee","Marty said no dogs in the store, he said it very firmly - he pointed","Marty","I also took a collar off my own rack for him and didn't charge myself - I'm not proud of it","Dee","His name is Wendell, he doesn't bark, which is the only reason he gets to stay - he just leans on your leg until you share","Marty","He is the best employee this feed store has ever had - I've told him so to his face"}},
{"r5_obit_mail_slot_three_notes","obituary",20,120,6,21,1,{"Marty","Three notes came through the mail slot this week for the death notices - I'll read them as written","Marty","The first says, 'Beverly Kidd, of March Ridge, she let every kid on Pine Street pick one tomato off her vines each summer - only one - she counted'","Marty","The second: 'My brother Terry Lusk wasn't a good man most of his life - on the ninth of July he was, so read that day'","Dee","That one's in pencil, it's been erased and written over two or three times","Marty","The third one is from a child, I think, it says, 'Buster - he was a dog, he counts.' And he does - Buster counts","Marty","If you want a name read, put it through the slot - you don't have to knock, just put it through"}},
{"r5_joke_maxine_buttermilk_pie","caller_joke",20,250,17,22,1,{"Caller - Maxine","Dee, you asked for recipes, so I've got my mother's buttermilk pie","Dee","Go ahead, Maxine","Caller - Maxine","You'll want two cups of sugar, a stick of butter, three eggs, and... hold on, honey - there's one at the kitchen window","Dee","Maxine?","Caller - Maxine","Sorry, sorry about that - it's gone on - where was I?","Dee","Three eggs","Caller - Maxine","Three eggs, a cup of buttermilk, now for the crust, use lard, and don't handle it too much - you want cold hands","Caller - Maxine","My hands are plenty cold right now, so this ought to be a real good crust"}},
{"r5_obit_dee_irene_butterscotch","obituary",20,200,0,5,1,{"Dee","I want to read a name for somebody who never had a single visitor","Dee","Miss Irene Stamper, ninety-three, she was on my hall at work for four years - couldn't get out of bed, sharp as a tack","Dee","Every night at three, when I came to turn her, she'd slip a butterscotch out from under her pillow and drop it in my scrub pocket - nobody ever brought her anything, I never did figure out where she got them","Dee","I found one in my pocket in August, it must have been in there since the ninth","Dee","It's still in my pocket, I'm not going to eat it"}},
{"r5_host_kayla_crayon_drawing","host",20,200,0,23,1,{"Marty","Somebody put something through the mail slot this morning, a drawing, in crayon, on the back of one of my feed invoices","Marty","It's this storeroom, I believe, there's a tower with lightning bolts coming off it and two stick people inside","Dee","One of the stick people has a big gray mustache, and he's frowning","Marty","I don't have a mustache","Dee","No, but you've got the frown","Marty","It's signed Kayla, age six - Kayla, it's going on the wall right beside the transmitter - thank you, sweetheart"}},
{"r5_joke_russell_further_instructions","caller_joke",20,150,17,22,1,{"Caller - Russell","Marty, back in July an Army helicopter dropped leaflets over my place","Marty","I remember those","Caller - Russell","It says, 'Remain calm, stay indoors, and await further instructions'","Caller - Russell","I have remained, I have stayed, I have awaited, I am the calmest man in Knox County","Marty","And the instructions?","Caller - Russell","Nothing, at this point, Marty, I'd settle for lesser instructions"}},
{"r5_joke_norris_fence_staples","caller_joke",20,140,17,22,1,{"Caller - Norris","Marty, I still owe you forty-two dollars on account, fence staples, from June","Marty","Norris, I don't believe that account matters anymore","Caller - Norris","It matters to me, I've been carrying it around like a rock in my boot","Marty","Then consider us square","Caller - Norris","Thank you, and now that we're square, I can finally say it - those staples were garbage, Marty"}},
{"r5_obit_caller_amber_papaw_truck","obituary",20,250,8,21,1,{"Caller - Amber","Hi - I'm fifteen - is it okay if I read somebody?","Dee","Of course it is, sweetheart - take your time","Caller - Amber","My papaw, Everett Hale, of Irvington, he let me drive his truck around the church parking lot on Sunday afternoons - he put a phone book on the seat so I could see over the wheel","Caller - Amber","He'd say, 'Easy on her, she's older than your mama'","Caller - Amber","I drive it for real now, for the family - I still sit on the phone book","Dee","Everett Hale, you drive careful, Amber"}},
}
